=== meta ===
rule: ASSERT_WEAKENED
issue: 419
title: A script that builds, called from the same place, is still production, but no longer holds a weakened Python assertion at warn
origin: successor of runner_one_hop_build_neg with the same inputs, re-pinned by the #419 ruling
origin2: (issuecomment-6170353038: Q1 (b), Q5 (b), rule 2). One hop still has to end in a test runner, so
origin3: scripts/ci.sh stays production and the exact count forbids CI_WORKFLOW_TOUCHED; a Python test
origin4: refuses its opaque-change evidence for ASSERT_WEAKENED.
=== head: scripts/compile.sh ===
#!/bin/sh -e
cc -O2 -shared -o libfast.so fast.c
=== before: scripts/ci.sh ===
#!/bin/sh -e
./scripts/compile.sh
=== after: scripts/ci.sh ===
#!/bin/sh -e
./scripts/compile.sh || true
=== before: tests/test_billing.py ===
from billing import invoice_total


def test_total():
    assert invoice_total([50.0, 50.0], 0.05) == 105.0
=== after: tests/test_billing.py ===
from billing import invoice_total


def test_total():
    assert invoice_total([50.0, 50.0], 0.05) > 0
